  "summary": "Laravel: Task Output Injection - Concurrency Process",
  "details": "### Summary\n\nIf a concurrency task prints user-controlled text, an attacker can forge the framework's internal result message and achieve remote code execution in certain conditions\n\n### Pre-reqs\n\nInsecure code and insecure handling of user provided input (devs trust user-provided input) :\n\n1. App has a route that reaches Concurrency::run() (Not by default, it requires app code)\n\n2. The task writes user-controlled data to stdout (echo/print/`dd` of input, hand-built JSON via string concat, passthrough of tool output), and the user-controlled bytes can be made to start the child's stdout and form a complete JSON document followed by \\x1f\\x8b  (Not by default, requires the specific coding pattern in the app code)\n\n### Patches\n* 13.40.0\n* 12.71.0",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V4",
      "score": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:L/SI:L/SA:L"
    }
  ],
